Generic single-database configuration.

env.py reads DATABASE_URL from app.core.config.get_settings() rather than
from alembic.ini, so the connection string lives in one place (.env).

    docker-compose exec backend alembic upgrade head

Or from the host (note `localhost`, not the docker service name `postgres`):

    cd backend
    DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/private_data_assistant \
        alembic upgrade head
